This course is an Introductory course on Human trafficking.
The objectives of this course are:
to bring about awareness and provide comprehensive understanding about   human trafficking amongst the masses;
develop functional understanding and coordination among learners about various stakeholders / agencies associated with the process of human trafficking directly or indirectly;
prepare well informed and updated professional  working in the government agencies ,Anti-Human Trafficking Units,  civil society organization, ,Para military and Military personnel’s, doctors, psychologists, lawyers ,judges and corporate sectors so that they are able to prevent, rehabilitate and re-integrate trafficked victims;
To educate and motivate the learners about establishing Human Trafficking Clubs in their family groups, society and institutions and create models of Community Policing in their Area.
Course Credit - 4

